WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:05.531
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie since I did a
villains power ranking for Arrow this year

00:00:05.531 --> 00:00:07.500
I wanted to do one for The Flash.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.500
I’m doing videos for both, so hopefully
I’ll be able to do this kind of thing all

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.500
year.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.790
Both Arrow and The Flash have only shot about
half their seasons so far.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:20.240
And the flash hasn’t officially been picked
up for a full season.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.640
So there are still a ton of villains both
shows can bring on.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:31.140
I might have to revise this list in February
when everything comes back from break.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:38.510
Since everything they’re doing is adapted
from a comic book I’ll try to not include

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:45.371
too many spoilers, but I’ll be explaining
each of these villains and their origin stories.

00:00:45.371 --> 00:00:46.371
So just a heads up.

00:00:46.371 --> 00:00:50.090
Starting with number 10 - Girder who we’ll
meet on the show as Tony Woodward

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:55.260
He’s being played by Greg Finley on the
show and we’ll meet him in episodes 6 and

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.260
7.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.070
In the comics he’s a normal blue collar
steel worker who gets thrown into a vat of

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:04.500
molten steel.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:12.300
The vat contained scraps of metal from star
labs experiments.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:17.190
The scraps convert his body into living Iron
giving him super strength and super durability.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.220
He becomes a walking tank.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.319
But because he’s iron, he can still rust.

00:01:21.319 --> 00:01:26.170
He was part of the appropriately titled Iron
Heights storyline in the comics, so that might

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.210
be how the tv series uses him.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:31.350
When people in the canon refer to Iron Heights,
they’re usually talking about Iron Heights

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.470
penitentiary, the big prison in Central City.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.980
The show might change his backstory just a
little but his powers will be the same.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.850
Number 9 - Plastique who we’ll meet on the
show as Bette Sans

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:45.610
She’s being played by Kelly Frye and we’ll
meet her in Episode 5.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:50.370
The character actually appeared in the Firestorm
Comics first.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:55.069
She was at times in love with Captain Atom
and his enemy.

00:01:55.069 --> 00:01:57.500
And eventually she was even part of the Suicide
Squad.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.479
So she’s one of the few easy crossover characters.

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:05.739
I know everyone’s asking about a suicide
squad show but I’ll mention something about

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:08.259
that at the end of the video.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:12.970
Because she’s a Firestorm-centric character,
she might get tied up in a Robbie Amell heavy

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:13.970
episode.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.300
He’s playing Firestorm on the show.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.250
Her ability allows her to project explosive
force from her body.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:23.730
So it might look like a concussion wave for
anyone that played Knights of the Old Republic.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:28.480
She was originally a suicide bomber in the
comics so they might change her backstory

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.110
on the show too.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:36.720
8 - Killer Frost because this could be potentially
super spoilery I’m just going to give an

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.720
extra warning with this tag.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.490
You can just jump forward in the video till
you don’t see this little tag if you want.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:44.000
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.740
Killer Frost is Caitlin Snow, on the show
that character is being played by Danielle

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:48.780
Panabaker.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.370
She is one of Barry’s friends.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:54.130
So it’s possible something big could happen
to make her turn against Team Flash.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:58.790
Her powers are pretty simple, she’s like
a female iceman.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:07.580
The reason I put her above the others is because
the smarter villains tend to be the more dangerous

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:08.580
ones.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.940
Okay, spoilers over, Number 7 - General Wade
Eiling who’s being played by Clancy Brown

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.520
He’s done a billion cartoon superhero voices,
you guys will really like him.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.890
He’s just an awesome actor in general.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.420
His character in the comics is actually responsible
for the creation of Captain Atom, so hopefully

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.290
we’ll see him on the show eventually.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:33.520
They’ve done a lot of different things with
the Wade character in the comics and cartoons.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.930
He’s transferred his consciousness into
another body, he’s injected himself with

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.440
Super Soldier Serum.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.010
On the show he’ll just be a sinister military
man throwing his weight around.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.290
But it’s possible they could make him all
hulked out.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.819
He’s like the DC Version of General Ross
from the Marvel Universe, so I don’t think

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:53.120
they need to give him powers to make him a
threat.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.550
Number 6 - Simon Stagg who will be played
by William Sadler

00:03:55.550 --> 00:04:00.200
We’re into mastermind slash big villain
territory now.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:05.560
As the list gets higher, the villains get
smarter and more dangerous.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:09.660
Simon Stagg is a super rich businessman in
the comics, so think of him as a Lex Luthor

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.660
type.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:14.340
He doesn’t have special powers of his own,
but he has unlimited money and is really good

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.849
at manipulating people.

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:20.239
I’m interested to see if in the show he
tries to hire any or all of the Rogues to

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:21.650
take down The Flash.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:27.760
There’s a lot more cool stuff in the comics,
his character is also kind of responsible

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.530
for the creation of Metamorpho.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:32.870
So that’s another character that The Flash
could bring on someday.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:36.280
Or they could be laying groundwork for The
Outsiders in a future season.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:39.530
Arrow’s already doing Katana this year,
so they’re part of the way there already.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.400
Number 5 - Heat Wave who we’ll meet on the
show as Mick Rory

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.780
He’s being played by Dominic Purcell, one
of the many Prison Break alums Arrow and The

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.780
Flash have cast.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:52.751
Because they’re doing powers on the show,
I think they’ll go with the new 52 version

00:04:52.751 --> 00:04:57.050
of the character, but give him the arc from
Flash Rebirth.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:01.820
Before the new 52 reboot, he had to use heat
guns to make flame and after the reboot he

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.130
became a full blown meta human.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:06.530
In the comics, Heat Wave has always been one
of the less dependable Rogues.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:10.680
So I think they cast Dominic Purcell because
he’s known for playing really powerful characters

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.430
that aren’t always the sharpest knife in
the drawer.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:18.050
He and Captain Cold have a very toxic relationship
as far as partners go, but Captain Cold is

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:23.480
definitely the brains of that Operation.

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:26.540
4 - The Clock King from Arrow

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.720
Robert Knepper is going to be a crossover
villain in episode 7.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.640
The Clock King will show up in Central City.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.250
Because episode 7 is also the episodes Girder
shows up in, it’s possible the two villains

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.800
could be connected somehow.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.699
Robert Knepper is also of course one of the
many Prison Break Alums, which leads me to

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:46.889
Number 3 - Captain Cold who we’ll meet on
the show as Leonard Snart

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:51.550
He’s being played by Wentworth Miller from
Prison Break.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.600
He’ll be in the fourth episode.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:56.560
Which is one episode after Robbie Amell debuts
as Firestorm.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.970
They really aren’t wasting any time rolling
out the big guns this season.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:05.570
Captain Cold will probably be a similar situation
to Heat Wave, they’ll give him his metahuman

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:10.979
abilities like in the new 52 comics but they’ll
be using classic elements of his backstory.

00:06:10.979 --> 00:06:14.540
The character isn’t straight up evil, he’s
more a villain of circumstance.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:19.350
The Flash has been able to reason with him
at times and the other Rogues have turned

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.970
on him for going against them.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:26.010
Wentworth Miller isn’t really known for
playing villains, so re-watch some of his

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.800
prison break episodes of you want to get a
vibe for what he might be like on The Flash.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.389
I know a lot of you are asking whether or
not The Flash will do his sister Glider.

00:06:36.389 --> 00:06:39.520
It’s possible, in the new 52 comics she
shows up after they wind up in prison.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:42.550
So she might get referenced if they don’t
cast an actor as her character.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.690
I’m really excited to see Captain Cold on
the show.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:50.690
He’ll be one of the better antagonists.

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:53.790
Number 2 - Professor Zoom

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:57.060
Yes I do think Professor Zoom will be a part
of the show somehow.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.419
If you’ve seen the first episode, please
use spoiler tags when commenting.

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:04.970
You can’t do a Flash show without the biggest
Flash villain ever, especially since they’re

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:06.400
sticking to the comics.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:14.259
So I don’t consider talking about Professor
Zoom to be a spoiler.

00:07:14.259 --> 00:07:23.259
At the TCAs, Greg Berlanti and Andrew Kriesberg
said we would learn about the big villain

00:07:23.259 --> 00:07:24.419
before the mid-season finale.

00:07:24.419 --> 00:07:28.070
So he’ll start appearing fairly quickly.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:29.860
No idea what that ends up looking like.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:33.590
But again, you can always read Flash Rebirth.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:42.100
Of all the Reverse Flashes, he’s the most
recognizable, but he’s not the most powerful.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:08:02.949
Which leads me to my number 1 villain on The
Flash this season - Zoom

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:07.330
Yes, I think we’ll see more than one Reverse
Flash.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.120
They will be two different people.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.650
I have my theories about how that’s going
to happen, but just to avoid super spoilers

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:17.580
I’ll wait till we get into episodes to talk
in depth about it.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.350
If you think about the characters they’ve
already announced, you’ve seen the Pilot

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:25.639
Episode and you read the comics and know how
Zoom becomes Zoom, think about which character

00:08:25.639 --> 00:08:27.890
on the show that might end up being.

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:32.940
I’ll give you a hint, it’s the one character
that hasn’t been doing any press and hasn’t

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.409
been going to any of the big conventions.

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:39.029
Let me know though, which of the Rogues are
you most excited to see and do you think they’ll

00:08:39.029 --> 00:08:41.419
make any prison break jokes if they appear
on screen together?

00:08:41.419 --> 00:08:47.050
I know the big question you have is how close
to the comics they’re sticking and Berlanti

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:50.860
and Kriesberg who are running the show said
that they’ll stick very close to the storyline

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.540
of Flash Rebirth with a few minor adjustments.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:57.920
Since I’m doing an Arrow Hero Power Ranking
Video Next Week I’ll do one for the Flash

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:58.930
too.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.800
If you’re new to my channel and you like
talking about Arrow and The Flash please subscribe

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.800
to get everything.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:04.060
We’d love to have you on the team.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:09.100
I’ll be doing videos for all the DC Comics
TV Shows, I’m really excited about everything.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:14.439
It’s going to be a lot of fun.

00:09:14.439 --> 00:09:20.730
Right now click here for my breakdown of the
new Arrow Season 3 Clip and click here to

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:23.800
learn about the Arrow Flash Crossover Episode.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:28.300
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and meet back up for some Star Wars tomorrow!

